Z||000000||triker||04-26-2000||07:07 PM||||I know everyone is trying to find ways to make their Fiero go just a little faster, and there are many questions about 3.1's, 3.4's and V8's, but having a complete Fiero 2.8 just laying around in my garage with a spun rod bearing, boring it out and putting in a 3.1 crank (and flex plate) seems to be the way for me to go.  My question is: Has anybody done this and are they happy with the results? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||04-26-2000||07:41 PM||||I know I'm not the only one who has done it and I am extremely happy with it.  Now notice that I only have around 600-700 miles on the new engine now, but it performs beautifully.<P>I don't (personal opinion inserted here) think that I have a huge amount of gain over the stock 2.8 (when it was brand new), but I can definitely tell a difference over an older engine.  It just seems peppier to me.<P>Haven't dynoed it or anything like that.<P>I've already gotten a 27mpg trip out of it (notice that mine is a 5spd)||||reg||1
